  "Currency": "Karensi",
  "Custom tier": "Level We Yu Seleftem",
  "Daily Nous reports on a retracted Journal of Medical Ethics submission containing multiple fabricated, AI-hallucinated references — complete with fake university affiliations and defunct email addresses — that the author reportedly left uncorrected even after being given a chance to fix proofs. The piece contrasts this with Bioethics, whose automated reference-checking would have caught the problem, and argues the real bottleneck isn't detection technology (one commenter's script flagged the fake citations in under a minute) but unpaid reviewer labor and publishing incentives that reward throughput over scrutiny.": "Daily Nous i ripotem wan pepa we oli bin submitim long Journal of Medical Ethics be biaen oli ritraktem, we i gat plante reference we oli feksem mo we AI i halusinetem — kam wetem giaman afiliesen blong iunivesiti mo email adres we i no eksis moa — mo raeta i lego olgeta i no stretem, evenwe oli bin givim jans blong hem stretem ol pruf. Stori i putum hem agens Bioethics, we sistem blong jekem reference blong hem otomatikli save bin kasem problem ia, mo i agiu se trufala bottleneck i no teknoloji blong faenemaot (wan skrip blong wan man we i komen i bin flagem ol giaman sitaesen insaed wan minit nomo) be i wok we ol revieweman oli mekem wetaot pem, mo ol insentiv blong pablisim we oli rewodim spid winim kea gud.",
  "Data free-riding vs. trillion-dollar AI valuations": "Yusum Data Wetaot Pem Long Hem, agensem Valu Blong AI We i Kasem Trilion Dola",
  "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI": "DeepMind CEO calls for an independent standards body to regulate frontier AI",
  "Demis Hassabis proposed a FINRA-style regulator for frontier model releases: labs would submit models for review up to 30 days before deployment, voluntary at first, with a path toward mandatory compliance in the US market.": "Demis Hassabis i propozem wan regiuleta olsem stael blong FINRA blong ol frontia moddel taem oli releas: ol lab bae oli submitim moddel blong revyu kasem 30 dei bifo deploymen, blong stat i voluntari nomo, wetem wan rod i go kasem komplaens we i mandatori long maket blong US.",
  "Denied": "I No Oke",
  "Deployable policy starter template": "Templet Blong Stat Polisi We Yu Save Deployem",
  "Deployable policy starter template at /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — a minimal static site with the full machine-readable layer, ready for Cloudflare Pages or any static host.": "Templet blong stat polisi we yu save deployem, long /downloads/agiright-policy-starter.zip — wan minimol stetik sait wetem fulwan level we masin i save ridim, redi blong Cloudflare Pages no eni stetik host.",
  "Deploying machine-readable policies on your site": "Deployem Ol Polisi We Masin i Save Ridim Long Sait Blong Yu",
  "Disclaimer": "Diskleima",
  "Distinct from human UI, SEO, or plain APIs, the AI Ingestion & Capability Layer gives websites a machine-facing architecture: a Manifest Layer (entry points like /llms.txt and /ai/manifest.json), a Corpus Layer (machine-readable knowledge), a Capability Layer (agent-callable tools), and a Governance Layer (provenance, licensing, versioning). Static-first, upgradeable toward APIs and MCP. Note: in this paper AICL names the ingestion architecture; on this site's protocol pages AICL refers to the AI Content Licensing Layer.": "I defren long UI blong man, SEO, no simpol API, AI Ingestion & Capability Layer i givim ol wesaet wan achitekja we i fesem masin: Manifest Layer (ol entri point olsem /llms.txt mo /ai/manifest.json), Corpus Layer (save we masin i save ridim), Capability Layer (ol tul we ejent i save singaotem), mo Governance Layer (wea i kamaot, laesensing, vesin namba). Stetik fastaem, be yu save apgredem i go long API mo MCP. Notis: long pepa ia AICL i minim achitekja blong ingestion; long ol pej blong protokol blong sait ia, AICL i minim Level blong Laesensing blong AI Kontent.",
  "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm": "Do Large Language Models Possess a Theory of Mind? A Comparative Evaluation Using the Strange Stories Paradigm",
  "Docs": "Dokumen",
  "Docs / Examples": "Dokumen / Eksampol",
  "Document library": "Laebrari Blong Dokumen",
  "Does AI have rights — and which framings are even coherent?": "AI i gat raet o nogat — mo wanem ol framing oli mekem sens stret?",
  "Download": "Daonlod",
  "Draft status": "Stetas Blong Draft",
  "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026": "EU AI Act: What Actually Applies on 2 August 2026",
  "Educational demo: HMAC-SHA256 with a shared secret, showing request-bound, expiring, verifiable license tokens. Production tokens should be signed asymmetrically, with the publisher’s public key discoverable under /.well-known/.": "Demo blong lanem save: HMAC-SHA256 wetem wan sikret we tufala i sherem, i soem ol token blong laesens we oli taengem long risik, oli save expaea, mo yu save vereifae. Ol token blong prodaksen oli sud saenem long asimetrik fasin, wetem pablik ki blong pablisa we yu save faenemaot aninit long /.well-known/.",
  "Eight more /topics entries, this time researched by an AI agent rather than curated by hand — same rule as before: every source fetched and confirmed live, summaries an original paraphrase, before anything gets added. 14 entries total.": "Eit moa entri long /topics, taem ia wan AI ejent i risejim, i no wan man i kiuretem wetem han — semfala rul olsem bifo: evri sos oli fej mo konfemem se i laef, ol sammari oli orijinol parafres, bifo eni samting i kasem adem. 14 entri altugeta.",
  "Email": "Imel",
  "Emotion Concepts and Their Function in a Large Language Model": "Emotion Concepts and Their Function in a Large Language Model",
  "Empirical Research": "Impirikol Risej",
  "English edition →": "Inglis Edisen →",
  "Ensure openness is machine-executable — so goodwill is not discarded as legal uncertainty.": "Mekem sua se openes i save ranem long masin — mekem se gudfala tingting i no lus olsem legol antaseten.",
  "Epistemology": "Epistemoloji",
