  "now": "naoia",
  "quotation — excerpt limits and attribution rules": "kwotesen — limit blong eksapt mo rul blong atribusen",
  "rag_use — retrieval-augmented generation, retention windows": "rag_use — retrieval-augmented generation, windo blong holem save",
  "read_access — whether AI may fetch and read the content": "read_access — sipos AI i save fejem mo ridim kontent",
  "redistribution — republishing or redistributing content or derivatives": "redistribution — pablisim bakegen no seraot bakegen kontent no ol samting we i kamaot long hem",
  "research pages & whitepapers": "ol pej blong risej mo waet pepa",
  "robots.txt and llms.txt govern access and visibility, not learning depth or use permissions. AIRS proposes expressing AI rights as a proportional, use-specific spectrum across ten dimensions — access, indexing, inference input, embedding, training, fine-tuning, distillation, memory, output, attribution/compensation. AILP translates this into /ai/rights-spectrum.json, letting creators declare granular permissions with compensation models ranging from free through license-required to revenue share.": "robots.txt mo llms.txt oli gavenem akses mo fasin blong luk, i no dip blong lanem save no pemisen blong yusum. AIRS i propozem blong talemaot raet blong AI olsem wan spektrom we i proposon mo spesifik long yusum, akros ten dimenson — akses, indeksing, input blong inferens, embedding, trening, fantuning, distilesen, memori, aotput, atribusen/pemen. AILP i tanem hemia i go long /ai/rights-spectrum.json, i letem ol kriata i talemaot ol pemisen wan wan wetem ol model blong pemen we i stat long fri i go kasem laesens-i-nidim i go kasem seraot mane.",
  "schema-invalid": "schema i no valid",
  "schema-valid": "schema i valid",
  "site guide for AI systems": "gaed blong sait blong ol sistem AI",
  "summarization — summaries, with or without attribution": "summarization — sammari, wetem o wetaot atribusen",
  "this site’s AI content rights policy": "polisi blong raet blong AI kontent blong sait ia",
  "this site’s license catalog": "katalog blong laesens blong sait ia",
  "training / fine_tuning / distillation — model internalization tiers": "training / fine_tuning / distillation — ol level blong internalaesesen blong moddel",
  "training — model training and fine-tuning permission": "training — pemisen blong trenem moddel mo fantuning",
  "transformation — structured extraction and derivative works": "transformation — tekemaot wetem straktja mo ol wok we oli kamaot long hem",
  "undeclared — high-risk pipelines may exclude": "undeclared — ol paeplaen we oli hae risik oli save iksklud",
  "verbatim_memory — whether exact reproduction is permitted": "verbatim_memory — sipos i oke blong ripodius stret semfala",
  "versioned, citable, traceable": "gat vesin namba, yu save sitem, yu save trakem",
  "“AICL: AI Ingestion & Capability Layer” now published in English as the canonical edition; the Chinese original manuscript remains available and both versions cross-link.": "“AICL: AI Ingestion & Capability Layer” naoia oli pablisim long Inglis olsem kanonikol edisen; orijinol Jaenis manuskrip i stap yet, mo tufala vesin oli konektem wanwan i go long ol nara.",
  "“Protocolized Openness” confirmed as an English-language paper (with Chinese parallel passages) — no separate translation planned.": "“Protocolized Openness” oli konfemem olsem wan pepa long Inglis lanwis (wetem ol parolel pasej long Jaenis) — i no gat wan seperet translesen we oli planem.",
  "↑ live machine-readable policy of this site": "↑ polisi we masin i save ridim, blong sait ia, i ranem naoia",
